 "caveats": [
  "Our share uses TID 10-17 at 15\" cells; the official Seabed 2030 figure counts cells with data at depth-dependent resolution (100 m to 800 m), so the two are not expected to match.",
  "TID codes change between releases for reasons other than new surveys (re-gridding, a data set re-classified as pre-generated grid or interpolation); cells can stop being 'measured'.",
  "One ocean mask (GEBCO_2026) for every year: coastline / ice-shelf changes between releases are ignored.",
  "1' cells count as measured if any 15\" sub-cell is; this overstates area if used for sums, so use stats."
